# Red on HEAD — fix-portability-value-set-and-preconditions

HEAD at the time of these runs: `d1f930e03ea6d5f87d262c44c12f3b55debb2619`
(`fix: fix-issue-filing-state-namespace (#179)`). Every run is offline: no token, no Gradle, no device.
The two readings below are reproduced from `git archive HEAD`, so nothing here depends on an uncommitted
edit.

## Issue #172 — the two readings a wrong root produced (pristine HEAD, 21 cases)

### Reading A — a git-archive export outside a git working tree (`/tmp/ci-verify`)

```
$ bash tools/check-portability.sh
check-portability: not inside a git working tree — pass --root <dir>
exit=2
$ bash tools/check-portability-selftest.sh
PASS portability#plantedRepoNameFails
PASS portability#plantedCategoryFails
PASS portability#excludesTheAdapterAndFixtures
PASS portability#valueSetIsReadNotHardCoded
  the check passes on the real tree: check-portability: not inside a git working tree — pass --root <dir>: expected '0', got '2'
FAIL portability#passesOnTheRealTree
...
check-portability-selftest: 1 of 21 cases failed
exit=1
```

The check refuses (`exit 2`), but the **suite reports the refusal as a failed case**.

### Reading B — a copy under a machine-local path (`<repo>/.pi/snapshot-172`)

```
$ cd .pi/snapshot-172 && bash tools/check-portability.sh
check-portability: OK — 42 engines and 2 templates name no project value (133 value(s) read from the project)
exit=0
$ bash tools/check-portability-selftest.sh
  the fixture lives in the machine-local state
FAIL foreign#fixtureIsVersioned
check-portability-selftest: 1 of 21 cases failed
exit=1
```

The check passes; the suite's own fixture case fails **by design**, because the fixture's versioned-path
assertion sees `/.pi/` in the root it was copied to.

## The cases written for this change, red on HEAD

### `tools/check-portability-selftest.sh` — `5 of 26 cases failed`

```
$ bash tools/check-portability-selftest.sh
FAIL portability#plantedValueInEveryNamespaceFails
FAIL portability#plantedSubmodulePathFails
FAIL portability#authorisationLabelIsTheOneException
FAIL preconditions#refusesOutsideAGitTree
FAIL preconditions#refusesUnderMachineLocalState
check-portability-selftest: 5 of 26 cases failed
```

Each case, with the reason HEAD gives:

```
$ bash tools/check-portability-selftest.sh --case 'portability#plantedValueInEveryNamespaceFails'
  the planted agent value is named: ''eligible'' not found in: check-portability: FAIL tools/issues/list.sh:164:PROBE_category="build-and-harness": names the project value 'build-and-harness' (tools/tooling.json namespaces.category)
check-portability: 1 leak(s) — a project value belongs in a config, never in an engine
FAIL portability#plantedValueInEveryNamespaceFails

$ bash tools/check-portability-selftest.sh --case 'portability#plantedSubmodulePathFails'
  loop.conf declares no LOOP_SUBMODULE_PATH — the submodule path has no home
FAIL portability#plantedSubmodulePathFails

$ bash tools/check-portability-selftest.sh --case 'portability#authorisationLabelIsTheOneException'
check-portability: OK — 42 engines and 2 templates name no project value (133 value(s) read from the project)
FAIL portability#authorisationLabelIsTheOneException

$ bash tools/check-portability-selftest.sh --case 'preconditions#refusesOutsideAGitTree'
FAIL preconditions#refusesOutsideAGitTree

$ bash tools/check-portability-selftest.sh --case 'preconditions#refusesUnderMachineLocalState'
  …: expected '2', got '0'
FAIL preconditions#refusesUnderMachineLocalState
```

`portability#plantedValueInEveryNamespaceFails` is the defect in one line: only the **category** value is
reported. `portability#plantedSubmodulePathFails` fails because the submodule path has no home in
`loop.conf`. `portability#authorisationLabelIsTheOneException` fails because the reserved label is read
from nowhere and asserted as nothing. The two `preconditions#…` cases fail because the suite runs its
cases (and reports red) instead of refusing.

### `tools/loop-selftest.sh` — `2 of 55 cases failed`

```
$ bash tools/loop-selftest.sh
  the device verdict is the value the profile's roles section declares: expected 'needs-a-device', got 'needs-device'
FAIL prescreen#readsTheVerdictsFromTheProfile
  the submodule the configuration names was not checked out: …
FAIL worktree#checksOutTheSubmoduleTheLoopConfigNames
loop-selftest: 2 of 55 cases failed
```

`prescreen#readsTheVerdictsFromTheProfile` renames `roles.deviceAgent` in the throwaway project's profile
and HEAD's pre-screen still says `needs-device` — the value is a literal in the engine, not a value read
at run time. `worktree#checksOutTheSubmoduleTheLoopConfigNames` declares the submodule at a path the loop's
configuration names, and HEAD's worktree names `app/src/main/cpp/libosmscout` instead, so the submodule is
not checked out.

